{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And Israel said, etc. And Elohim will be, etc.</b> The intent of his saying <b>I am dying</b>, etc. is that they should not suppose that at Jacob's death the Shekhinah would withdraw from among them — but even if he dies, Elohim will be with them. And his saying <b>and He will return</b>, etc. informed him that they would be remembered to restore their settlement without any doubt in the matter. And he was precise in saying <b>the land of your fathers</b>, for the land was given to the fathers and they merited it, not to those who leave Egypt; from this it follows that I have it in my power to give you one Shechem, etc., for by this the giving from him to him is justified — and that is his saying <b>and I have given you, etc.</b> And even according to the words of our Rabbis of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 97:6) that Shechem is as its literal meaning, that the sons of Jacob came upon its spoil — even so, apart from the merit of the fathers in the land, neither Jacob nor his sons would merit it."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:50:13.254313607Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}